# Line endings, decided once.
#
# Without this, what lands in a commit depends on each machine's core.autocrlf
# and on which tool last wrote the file. retention.mjs was committed as LF, a
# later edit wrote it back as CRLF, and the next `git add` staged the whole file
# as changed -- 669 added and 515 deleted for an edit that touched 154 lines.
# A diff that size hides its own content, which is the real cost.
#
# text=auto eol=lf: git decides what is text, stores it with LF, and checks it
# out with LF. Editors on Windows have handled LF for years, and every consumer
# of this repository -- Netlify's build, the functions, node -- is happier with
# it than with CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, so git never inspects or converts the bytes. A "text" file that is
# really an image gets its 0x0D bytes rewritten on checkout, and the result is
# a corrupt file that looks fine in a diff because git will not show it.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.ico  binary
*.pdf  binary

# Fonts. tools/builder/renderer/_fonts and public/builder/fonts hold the two
# licensed faces the print renderer loads explicitly, and a corrupted one does
# not fall back -- prepareScene throws rather than substituting, by design.
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary

# Media.
*.mp4 binary
*.webm binary
*.mov binary
